 ## Overview
-A volume rendering technique that casts rays from a viewing plane through a 3D voxel grid, sampling voxel values using barycentric interpolation within the unit cube, and accumulating lighting contributions (ambient, diffuse, specular) along the ray path [S1, unofficial]. It projects values to a view plane to produce a 2D image by casting parallel rays from the eye to voxels [S2, unofficial]. It is distinguished by the explicit use of barycentric interpolation for spatial sampling and the Phong shading model for lighting calculation, rather than simple nearest-neighbor or trilinear interpolation combined with standard transfer function opacity alone [S1, unofficial].
